bin/
dist/
coverage.out
coverage.html
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store

# What the end-to-end test leaves behind for a human to open. Evidence of a run,
# not part of the tree — and it is a real model's answer to a real prompt, so it
# is not something to commit by reflex.
e2e-artefacts/

# What `neverseen proxy -v` writes: both bodies of every exchange it saw, in
# clear. Evidence of one run and nothing else — and unlike the artefacts above,
# these hold somebody's real data, so committing one is a leak rather than noise.
traces/

# The browser extension's dependencies. Its lockfile is committed — CI installs
# from it with `npm ci` — and what that installs is not.
node_modules/

# An enrolment token, or anything else pasted beside the tree while working on
# supervision. The same reason `.env` is here: `git add -A` is one keystroke, and a
# token committed is a token to rotate.
.secrets
